INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: autonomy #S2.1: a code task behind a held work claim is re-polled and re-logged every tick (978 code-task.claim-held rows in 24 hours); skip it until the holder expires',
'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js
code-anchor: async function claimsSweep(env) {
code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js"], "contains": "CLAIM-HELD-PARK-1"}

Charter pillar autonomy (roadmap row RM-S2-EVENT-DRIVEN-1, qnfo-audit roadmap_implementation id 1; first slice of replacing time-triggered polling by wake-on-expiry). Metric to move: cloud_ops_events rows of kind code-task.claim-held per 24 hours (978 for 2026-11-03T12:00Z to 2026-11-04T12:00Z). Guards that must not worsen: code_task_success_rate_30d, code_pr_merge_share_7d.
Evidence (read 2026-11-04): claimsSweep runs on every tick over each queued code task that is not claim-fresh, calls claimTake and, on HTTP 409, counts held++ and writes one code-task.claim-held event. Nothing remembers the holder, so a task behind a file another session holds for an hour is retried and logged on every tick (62 tasks were queued; the event was the third most frequent kind of the day). CLAIM_WAIT_MS stays 2 minutes (SLA-COMPRESS-1) for the first deferral.
EDIT: in the 409 branch of claimsSweep record the holder and its expires_at on the task claim record, skip that task in later sweeps until min(expires_at, now + 20 minutes) with the wait doubling from CLAIM_WAIT_MS on each consecutive 409, and write the code-task.claim-held event once per (task, holder) instead of once per tick. A holder that releases early is noticed at the next unskipped sweep. Mark the change CLAIM-HELD-PARK-1, cover it in the orchestrator claim test, bump with scripts/worker_release.py.
Definition of done: merged and verified live: code-task.claim-held rows per 24 hours are at most 400 for a full day after the deploy, and code_task_success_rate_30d is not lower than before.',
'session:c5-engine', 'feature', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER), CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER)
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: autonomy #S2.1:%' AND status = 'open');

